   $q$How does the author develop the connection between Varga's idea and the dockworkers over the course of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The dockworkers resisted Varga's idea, and their resistance caused the six years of delay before it could work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The idea created so much new cargo that the port hired more dockworkers than it had ever employed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"An idea meant to save time at the pier cut the need for workers, and the union answered with retraining for new jobs.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Varga designed the idea mainly to protect dockworkers from injury, and the retraining was her own plan.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An idea meant to save time at the pier cut the need for workers, and the union answered with retraining for new jobs.$q$, $q$Varga's goal was saving time at the pier (paragraph 2), but paragraph 5 shows the result: far fewer workers were needed, and the union negotiated retraining. The delay came from weak piers and ships, not from worker resistance.$q$, 'draft', '1097d629-e255-5598-b986-4dde68f333d1')
