   $q$What led the rules committee to add a shot clock in 2014?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Turnovers had risen sharply because players rushed their passes late in games.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"},{"text":"Slow, low-scoring games had been followed by several seasons of shrinking attendance.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Coaches wanted a way to give playing time to more athletes on their benches.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"Players had complained that games without a shot clock were too tiring to play.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Slow, low-scoring games had been followed by several seasons of shrinking attendance.$q$, $q$Paragraphs 1 and 2 connect slow games like the 19 to 16 championship to "several seasons of shrinking attendance" before the vote. Rushed passes and longer benches were results of the clock, not reasons for it.$q$, 'draft', 'da7fbf7e-ec2e-5cef-accb-14b15de0c7e3')
