   $q$How does the winter finding in the final paragraph develop the passage's account of the roof program?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It qualifies the program's success by showing that its value depends on a city's balance of seasons.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It explains why the council chose to cover only half the cost of coating each building's roof.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It reverses the account by showing that the program cost Tessaro more than it saved over a full year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It proves that white roofs would work equally well in any city that copied Tessaro's exact approach.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It qualifies the program's success by showing that its value depends on a city's balance of seasons.$q$, $q$The final paragraph reports a real cost but notes that Tessaro's long summers outweigh it, and warns that cities with harsh winters "might reach a different conclusion." It limits the success rather than reversing it, since summer savings were "much larger."$q$, 'draft', 'b5c3a4e7-c9ae-58f6-9a60-95dfa2410554')
